### bare word between single-quoted parts
echo 'export TIMEOUT='30';'
>>> SC2026 1:23

### alphanumeric word between quoted sed fragments
sed 's/old/'new'/g' config.ini
>>> SC2026 1:13

### star after single quote is a glob
ls 'report'*
>>> none

### single-quoted value at end of word
wget --header='Accept: text/html' https://example.com
>>> none

### line continuation between single-quoted strings
printf '%s\n' 'first line' \
  'second line'
>>> none

### word after an ansi-c string
#!/bin/bash
echo $'a\t'b'c' pre$'two'post
>>> none
